      "message": "Trouble is if bpf_skb_pull_data succeeds in pulling sizeof(tcphdr) bytes, but by doing this it pulls from the second segment.\n\nConsider the case of a fragment GSO packet with UDP packets with 1B payload.\n\nWith fraglist, that has one IP + UDP header, either in skb linear or skb frags[], as is true for the 1st byte of payload. Then followed by up to 44 frag_list[] skbs each of 1B.\n\nIf we pull sizeof(struct iphdr) + sizeof(struct tcphdr) then we pull the IP and UDP headers plus 12 payload bytes. This will succeed, but the first 11 frag_list skbs are now pulled in, corrupting the fraglist GSO skb.",
